  "example_scope": "The existing public-facade/std Rust example now separates polling, dispatch and receipt acceptance across bounded host-owned turns. Two LocalVm instances borrow one immutable compiled IR but create distinct local owners, native state and original fuel meters. Original catalog compilation, capture, evaluation and reply-gated continuation remain unchanged. The queue is a headless single-threaded adapter, not a language scheduler or GUI toolkit integration.",
  "authority_scope": "Pending cancellation revokes before guarded native dispatch and commits nothing. Cancellation after mutation rejects the delayed receipt while preserving the already-applied effect. Revocation before acceptance follows the example host policy of failing only that instance, with no tail dispatch or rollback. A sibling finishes independently. Local owner/serial correlation is not an authenticated external transport or durable replay protocol.",
  "test_scope": "Six new test functions cover interleaving and exact immediate/queued fuel parity; both cancellation windows; live revocation; every insufficient fuel grant while a sibling runs at its exact completion grant; idle Awaiting polls and foreign/wrong-typed receipt ownership; and cancelled/dropped owners. All twelve tests run under native and reference features locally and unchanged in both exported package and independent consumer. Totals overlap; they are execution counts, not distinct features.",
